WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600 line:78% align:center
I'm an aviation maintenance technician,
which basically means I help keep

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.850 line:78% align:center
airplanes safe and ready to fly.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.050 line:78% align:center
My team works on airplanes, checking
everything from the engines, wings,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.870 line:78% align:center
and wheels to make sure it all
works properly.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.150 line:78% align:center
To become an aviation maintenance
technician, you need an A&P license,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.460 line:78% align:center
airframe, and power plant, which you can
earn through a two-year aviation

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.830 line:78% align:center
or technical school program.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.710 line:78% align:center
We highly recommend getting experience early
because employers really value

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.880 line:78% align:center
people who can work
confidently with tools.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:37.760 line:78% align:center
Good luck!
